※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4409 LANG_TYPEDEF_FIELD_OF_NOTHING

※ A product holds all of its fields, so one of a type that carries no
※ information leaves the product meaning what it would have meant without it.
※ A variant of a sum may be `void`, and the test beside this one writes one.

type Padded = a : u8 ; nothing : void

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
